{"questions":[{"question_id":"1lfxdzrvh","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2008 Paper 2 Offline","year":2008,"examDate":2008,"subject":"physics","chapter":"laws-of-motion","chapterGroup":"mechanics","topic":"friction-force","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"pstatement-1--it-is-easier-to-pull-a-heavy-object-than-to-jee-advanced-physics-motion-pyk80tblajc1c1pg","content":"<p>STATEMENT 1 : It is easier to pull a heavy object than to push it on a level ground.</p>\n<p>and</p>\n<p>STATEMENT 2 : The magnitude of frictional force depends on the nature of the two surfaces in contact.</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Statement 1 is True, Statement 2 is True; Statement 2 is a CORRECT explanation for Statement 1"},{"identifier":"B","content":"Statement 1 is True, Statement 2 is True; Statement 2 is a NOT CORRECT explanation for Statement 1"},{"identifier":"C","content":"Statement 1 is True, Statement 2 is False"},{"identifier":"D","content":"Statement 1 is False, Statement 2 is True"}],"correct_options":["B"],"explanation":"<p><b>Case I : Free body diagram.</b></p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1lgmqiida/46d3c048-508d-4b2a-9bfe-f84f7e7ef60f/026b69e0-de2a-11ed-8949-7f844f9a11f4/file-1lgmqiidb.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1lgmqiida/46d3c048-508d-4b2a-9bfe-f84f7e7ef60f/026b69e0-de2a-11ed-8949-7f844f9a11f4/file-1lgmqiidb.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2008 Paper 2 Offline Physics - Laws of Motion Question 8 English Explanation 1\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1lgmqiida/46d3c048-508d-4b2a-9bfe-f84f7e7ef60f/026b69e0-de2a-11ed-8949-7f844f9a11f4/file-1lgmqiidb.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1lgmqiida/46d3c048-508d-4b2a-9bfe-f84f7e7ef60f/026b69e0-de2a-11ed-8949-7f844f9a11f4/file-1lgmqiidb.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.